  "submission": {
    "op": "submit",
    "status": "answered",
    "diagnosis": "The shared LogPrinter path used by both logs and up attaches a streaming stdout/stderr reader without checking the container's TTY mode. The missing first eight bytes and delayed output are consistent with a raw TTY stream being treated as Docker's framed non-TTY stream by the underlying attach reader. split_buffer already yields complete lines immediately when its reader yields data, so its source does not explain the eight-byte loss. This is a likely protocol-boundary diagnosis; the external Docker client implementation and runtime behavior were not inspected or tested.",
    "proposed_change": "Select a raw streaming attachment for containers with Config.Tty enabled (using the available attach_socket path or a supported raw attach option), while preserving the existing framed path for non-TTY containers. Add a TTY regression that retains the first bytes and exposes the first line before exit, plus a non-TTY control. Verify the Docker-client socket/HTTP decoding requirements before implementing.",
